- op: discuss  # 9a9a
  at: '2026-09-20T05:25:18Z'  # 9a9a
  by: agent  # 9a9a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9a9a
  clock: 6  # 9a9a
  nonce: 9a9a  # 9a9a
  message: "DONE. ADR-0057 section 15 implemented as _absorb_partial_external_keys, a second phase inside the merge pass's _fold_edges, running after section 11's fold on identical (src, dst, edge_type) over what it left.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, on the committed scip-python recording (section 12 discipline — producer-shaped input, never the incumbent's output fed back). The syntax arm emits 7 module-less method-call stubs. Six are absorbed by the twin that states the module and survive as ONE edge carrying the stated module and both origins; the seventh (label, a property the SCIP arm resolves in-repo) has no twin stating a module, so nothing absorbs it and section 14's supersession applies instead, unchanged. Seven stubs in, one sentinel stub out.\n\nCounted from the other side by the backend-agreement instrument, external unresolved `calls` move from (2 both, 11 python-only, 6 scip-only) to (8 both, 5 python-only, 0 scip-only). The six typed twins that had no partner now have one. That zero is the row's point: before this, one call carried two edges and the typed one was invisible to any consumer counting sites.\n\nWHAT THE SURVIVOR CARRIES: incumbent-first; the stated dst_ref; dst rebuilt by format_legacy_dst; id re-minted through the newly extracted ir.mint_edge_id (ADR-0036 — an id derives from attributes, so a changed dst must re-mint); edge_key reset; origin unioned; call sites absorbed; confidence corroborated under section 13 where the pathways differ. attribution[\"dst_ref\"] names the stating producer and alternatives gains NO dst_ref entry, because the loser abstained and section 1 says an abstention contributes no entry at all.\n\nREFUSALS, tested: two partial keys never match each other; a different callee name, line or edge_type does not fold; one producer's two calls on a line are not a contradiction; an in-repo dst is untouched (section 14 owns that case); two complete candidates disagreeing on the module are reported on MergeReport.ambiguous rather than guessed, and candidates that AGREE on the module are not ambiguous.\n\nPLACEMENT, and why it is not finalize: deduplicate_edges has not run at the merge pass, so every edge is still one call site. After it a stub carries meta[\"call_lines\"] for N sites and absorbing it would assert the twin's module of all N — 12,126 external call edges on this repository are post-collapse multi-site, 4,818 of them sentinel-module.\n\nFull affected slice green (14 chunks, ~20,600 tests); 100% coverage on ir.py and merge_producers.py; docs/schema.json unchanged — attribution/alternatives already serialize and dst_ref already round-trips.\n\nNOT ASSERTED, per section 15.7: that the stated module is correct; that two same-named calls on one line are one call (10 of 86,839 site groups here are not, and the rule refuses); that a partial matches a partial; anything about a language whose second producer does not exist."  # 9a9a
